# High Noon: "Each player can't cast more than one spell each turn." Bot1 casts High Noon as its fourth spell of turn 1
# (nothing limits it before it is out), and is then refused a fifth (ruling: it has cast a spell this turn). Bot2's
# turn 2: one spell, a second refused. Turn 3: Bot1 casts one spell, a second is refused, then pays {4}{R} and
# sacrifices High Noon (an activated ability, not a spell, so the limit does not touch it): 5 damage to Bot2, and the
# limit is gone, so the second spell is cast at once.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Sol Ring
High Noon
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Plains x17

